**Database Implementation**

The following Java code implements a simple database using a HashMap to store data.

```java
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

public class Database {
    private Map<String, Object> data;

    public Database() {
        this.data = new HashMap<>();
    }

    // Insert a new row into the database
    public void insert(String id, String name) {
        data.put(id, name);
    }

    // Select rows from the database based on an SQL query
    public Iterator<Map.Entry<String, Object>> selectFromTable(String... params) throws Exception {
        for (Map.Entry<String, Object> entry : data.entrySet()) {
            boolean match = true;
            if (params != null && params.length > 0) {
                for (int i = 0; i < params.length; i++) {
                    if (!entry.getKey().equals(params[i])) {
                        match = false;
                        break;
                    }
                }
            } else if (params == null && !data.containsKey(entry.getKey())) {
                match = false;
            }

            if (match) {
                System.out.println("ID: " + entry.getKey() + ", Name: " + entry.getValue());
            }
        }

        return data.entrySet().iterator();
    }

    // Update a row in the database
    public void update(String id, String name) throws Exception {
        if (data.containsKey(id)) {
            data.put(id, name);
        } else {
            throw new Exception("Row not found");
        }
    }

    // Delete a row from the database
    public void delete(String id) throws Exception {
        if (data.containsKey(id)) {
            data.remove(id);
        } else {
            throw new Exception("Row not found");
        }
    }
}
```

**Example Usage**

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        Database db = new Database();

        // Insert rows into the database
        db.insert("1", "John");
        db.insert("2", "Jane");

        // Select rows from the database where 'name' is not 'John'
        db.selectFromTable("John");

        // Update a row in the database
        db.update("1", "John Updated");

        // Delete a row from the database
        db.delete("2");
    }
}
```

This code provides a basic structure for a database using a HashMap to store data. It includes methods for inserting, updating, and deleting rows in the database, as well as selecting rows based on an SQL query. The example usage demonstrates how to create a database, insert rows into it, select specific rows, update a row, and delete a row.
